coder › Implemented `RateLimiter` as a token bucket in `src/limiter.ts`.

What changed
- `src/limiter.ts`
  - Added private `tokens` (current amount, may be fractional) and `lastRefill` (ms timestamp from `now()`).
  - Constructor starts the bucket full at `capacity` and records the initial time.
  - `available` refills up to the current time and returns the fractional token count.
  - `tryTake(n = 1)` refuses `n > capacity` without touching state, refills first, then only deducts if `tokens >= n`.
  - Refill adds `(elapsedMs / 1000) * refillPerSecond`, clamped at capacity; negative clock skew is treated as zero elapsed.
- `src/limiter.test.ts`
  - Added 7 tests covering: starts full, explicit `n`, refusal with no side effects, oversized requests, continuous fractional refill, refill-before-take, and never exceeding capacity.

